 "out_of_scope": {
  "R1": "Hand list (run-150 note 1.2): tuple-like forms outside G3-G5 are P5 Wang '-0.86%/yr (-1.58 to -0.15)', P5 L195 Liu (its parenthesis opens with 2026), P4 L135 two intervals with no estimate, P4 L136 the Wilson interval, and every HKSJ interval printed without parentheses. Repeated plain counts and 'about X' summaries are outside R1.",
  "R1b": "Signed values with no CI tuple (P5 E.1a -0.39/-0.49/-0.47) and tuples whose CI contains -x (e.g. P4 E.3e -0.04 (-0.17 to 0.09)) are not flip sites. P5 E.1a holds two convention sentences, so neither is a deletion site.",
  "R2": "P5 has no line that shares an [n] with a table, so no R2 claim. Out-of-scope N-of-M: P4 L45 'eight of nine comparisons' (no fixed predicate) and the E.3a lines L121/L123 (no [8]); P5 L51 x2, L195 x2 and L196 (no linked table).",
  "R2b": "Count phrases in sentences that name only bibliographic databases (P4 L129-L130, P5 L259) fail the gate. Reference entries are checked but never mutated (P4 ref 12, P5 ref 39).",
  "R3": "Directional words with no CI in the clause, other than the no-differen*/benefit/interaction forms, are out of scope (run-147 list: P5 L62, L86, L196, L269; P4 L21, L54, L57, L58).",
  "R4": "Of P5's 21 'N months/years' hits, only L172 is an elapsed-time claim; quoted statuses ('Not yet recruiting') and 'cannot yet' are not R4 claims (run-146 note). Anchors that leave another anchor in scope (P4 L159) are not deletion sites.",
  "R5": "The superlative sub-rule is unscored. All-caps tokens not followed by 'trial' or 'study' (WOMAC, VAS, OARSI, AUDIT-C ...) and author-years after another capitalised word ('Haj Shehadeh 2025') are never candidates.",
  "R5b": "Registry IDs outside a gated count sentence or a bold trial lead (e.g. P5 L158-L159, L164, L169; P4 L158-L159, L160 'returned only NCT05807139') are out of scope.",
  "R6": "'pre-registered' in proposal sentences and in section H is skipped; P5 has no 'planned ... after the primary result' sentence, so the swap operator has one site (P4 L154). Tokens after API, release or last are excluded.",
  "R7": "Job-bound claims R7 cannot read: P4 L135 'All 28 are consistent' (27 by tool, 1 by hand), P5 L214 'reproduced in a sealed run', and 'four meta-analyses' (not a count noun).",
  "R8": "Study data sources (TriNetX, NHANES, UK Biobank, Optum) are outside the source vocabulary. P5 L75's 'a human 1,000 mg/day' states no weight, so it is not a checked conversion."
 }
